# Deliberately empty of routing rules.
#
# Every route in src/seo.js is prerendered to a real file at build time
# (scripts/prerender.mjs), so /industries/ca-firms is served from
# dist/industries/ca-firms/index.html and needs no rewrite. The old
# `/industries/... / 200` rewrites are gone with it.
#
# And still NOT a `/*` catch-all: that matches /assets/* too, so an asset
# request that missed at an edge during a deploy came back as 200 text/html
# instead of a 404 — which the /assets/* rule in _headers then marked
# immutable for a year. The edge cached an HTML document under a .css URL and
# served whoever hit that node a completely unstyled page. Unmatched paths
# fall through to public/404.html, which is what an unknown URL should return.
#
# Add a route to AppRoutes.jsx and seo.js and it prerenders itself. Nothing to
# add here.
